# iCloud Drive conflict copies ("Forecast 2.swift" beside "Forecast.swift") are NOT ignored
# here on purpose. A glob wide enough to catch them — `* [0-9].*` — also silently swallows
# "docs/Chapter 3.md", and a file that cannot be staged with no explanation is worse than one
# that gets caught loudly. `scripts/release.sh` refuses to release while any file whose name
# matches the conflict shape *and* has a same-named sibling is tracked, which is precise, and
# it says which files. That is the check; this is the note saying why there is no glob.
